  contentsAnswer: Books from my father, and his old camera. I could not bring myself
    to leave either behind.
  weightAnswer: Nine kilos, give or take. Books are heavier than they look.
  metalAnswer: The camera body is metal. It is wrapped in a shirt between the books.
  packingAnswer: Packed solid. There is not room for anything to roll around.
  responseAnswer: A dull tap would make sense. The camera is off and wedged in place.
  authorReasoning: 'Innocent: 9.2 kg, modest metal, no substantial pulse movement.
    No equipment specification knowledge needed.'
